{{interactive_demo:2}}

{{algorithm:2}}

{{demo:2}}

<details><summary>Reveal the counting proof</summary>

Since $2\operatorname{arsinh}(|n|/2)\le R$ exactly when $|n|\le2\sinh(R/2)$, the integral indices form a symmetric interval with $2\lfloor2\sinh(R/2)floor+1$ elements.

</details>

## Continue exploring

For background, see the [Poincare disk model](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poincar%C3%A9_disk_model), [modular group](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Modular_group), and [Selberg zeta function](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Selberg_zeta_function). These links provide context; all claims and derivations used in this presentation are stated above.

